ng of  secular because the corrupted monk is  infested with centipedes and centipedes  other thing that imparts immortality in  secular so the implication is that  priestess y'all can trace her  immortality to the carp that's infested  with centipedes below Fountainhead lake  just like a bikuni traces her  immortality to the knee no the corrupted  monk is not the only warrior monk we see  in game and in fact we get to see and  fight a great deal of them at semper  temple upon mount Kongo while this area  is a part of a Sheena and the monks are  known to interact with our sheena on  occasion these people are sort of a more  separate group rather than trusty  vassals of the state indeed similar  warrior monk groups actually existed in  medieval and feudal Japan they merged  during the Heian period fuelled by  really fundamental disagreements on  Buddhist teachings between temples and  at first these warrior monk groups cared  for nothing but fighting one another yet  with the flow of time they began to  accumulate power as well  again pay war even saw commanders giving  presents to temples as an attempt to get  these warrior monks to fight on their  side and that however only lasted until  the end of the sangoku period where  Tokugawa Ieyasu and Oda Nobunaga saw  warrior monks as a threat to the  government so they were the first to  directly oppose them as a result of  Tokugawa's efforts warrior monks ceased  to exist by the time he became Shogun in  the 17th century  and speaking of Tokugawa and his  administration the interior ministry in  secular is likely the greatest threat  that the land of our China has ever seen  in the final act of the game we see the  ministry's warriors cutting through the  samurai of oshina as if there were  nothing exterminating pretty much  everybody who stands in their way and  yet while the words interior ministry is  thrown around a lot the question of  whose  stands behind the actions of the  interior ministry is never raised or  never answered however there are certain  hints that the in-game interior ministry  are warriors of real-life Tokugawa  Ieyasu which is evidenced by several  things first the emblems on their armor  they look really similar to the Tokugawa  family crest and the red troops the  ACA's Ornette was an elite group under  the command of one of Tokugawa's  generals in real life and as for the  ministry itself we should note that the  Japanese word knife foo does not  actually even mean interior ministry  instead it means interior minister which  was a government title in Japan Tokugawa  Ieyasu  was actually an interior minister during  the final years of the single GU era  thus we can conclude that the ash in a  clan might not be fighting an  organization but rather a man and that  man was most likely Tokugawa this in my  opinion is a bit of a missed opportunity  to have a concrete antagonist for the  forces of the Hashanah instead of just  the shadowy interior ministry now that  we've talked about fashion as enemies  let's move on to their great hero  Ian's title the sword Saint is not just  this fancy turn of phrase  it's actually an existing honorary title  that was given only to the best of  swordsmen one of such saints in real  life is Ito et Ossa kaga heesu who might  have even served as an inspiration for  eachine little is known of Ito except  that he was an outstandingly skilled  combatant proficient with both sword and  spear and skilled to such an extent that  many actually considered his powers  supernatural but here's the main thing  one of the fundamental principles of  Vito's techniques was moussaka which is  reacting to the enemy's attack not as  this conscious effort but instead  reacting spontaneously without thinking  moussaka is similar to machine a  technique that shares its name with the  Machine esoteric texts developed by  yishun himself in game  so these two are also similar in the  sense that both of them actually named  sword techniques after thems